note: design 100 (R100.5-1): two nested `.await` in a coroutine body: the old `.await` pairs with the inner `.await` of the same source node, and the outer `.await` is the new point
rule+: R100.5-1
must_match: \+ await `fetch\(fetch\(a\)\.await\)\.await`
must_not_match: ~ await
=== both Cargo.toml
[package]
name = "shop"
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2021"
=== old src/lib.rs
pub async fn fetch(x: u32) -> u32 {
    x + 3
}

pub async fn sum(a: u32) -> u32 {
    fetch(a).await + 1
}
=== new src/lib.rs
pub async fn fetch(x: u32) -> u32 {
    x + 3
}

pub async fn sum(a: u32) -> u32 {
    fetch(fetch(a).await).await + 1
}
